/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A function hands back a `permanently` series; a rabbit's series is stored into what it handed back.

    What a cast hands back is no deeper than what it can reach, and a constant is as far out as
    anything (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Define table as a series of series of number permanently.
Bind series of series of number to get-table:
    Return table.
Done.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define xs as a series of number with (3, 2).
    Define k as cast get-table.
    Insert xs into k.
Done.
State table.
